  {
   "line": 77,
   "old": "\\par\\vspace{2pt}\\parbox{\\textwidth}{\\scriptsize IEA37 Case Study~1, 13-method pool (scenario: turbines, evaluations; random starts, 30 seed-paired runs). Feas./Rank: feasible runs and feasibility-aware rank of the mean AEP (fewer than 15 feasible runs = ranked below the qualified methods). Best: rank-1 method and its mean AEP (MWh) over its feasible runs; n.s.: methods not significantly different from the best method (seed-paired Wilcoxon signed-rank, infeasible runs below every feasible run, Holm over its 12 comparisons, $\\alpha=0.05$). Scenarios: stored labels; $^a$in each scenario the open runs with the highest AEP of each exact-gradient method are taken as infeasible until only 15 of its 30 runs remain feasible (the lowest mean it can have while ranked by its mean); open exact infeas.: every open exact-gradient label taken as infeasible; + open MS-SLSQP: in addition every open label of MS-SLSQP with finite-difference gradients (fin.\\ diff.) taken as infeasible; ex.: exact gradient. Benchmark (68 cases, eight methods): with all 448 open MS-SLSQP labels infeasible (67 cases, at most 16 per case), MS-SLSQP has 78.0\\% feasible runs and fewer than 15 feasible runs in 1 case; average ranks PSO-VNS 1.82$\\to$1.82, PSO 1.97$\\to$1.98, SSA-VNS 3.45$\\to$3.46, VNS 4.40$\\to$4.40, SSA 5.38$\\to$5.40, MS-SLSQP 5.88$\\to$5.82, LX-SSA 6.06$\\to$6.07, DE 7.04$\\to$7.05 (order unchanged); all-run outcome PSO-VNS vs.\\ MS-SLSQP 1649/218/173$\\to$1716/185/139 (wins/ties/losses). Horns Rev~1 pool (11 methods), open MS-SLSQP labels infeasible: 6{,}030 evaluations: 20 labels, MS-SLSQP 30$\\to$10 feasible runs, rank 8$\\to$10, best method PSO-VNS; 30{,}030 evaluations: 20 labels, MS-SLSQP 30$\\to$10 feasible runs, rank 8$\\to$10, best method GA. Budget and initialization studies: 22 case groups contain open MS-SLSQP labels; MS-SLSQP keeps at least half of its runs feasible in 18 of them and loses that qualification in 4 (Horns Rev~1).}",
   "new": "\\par\\vspace{2pt}\\parbox{\\textwidth}{\\scriptsize IEA37 Case Study~1, 13-method pool (scenario: turbines, evaluations; random starts, 30 seed-paired runs). Feas./Rank: feasible runs and feasibility-aware rank of the mean AEP (fewer than 15 feasible runs = ranked below the qualified methods). Best: rank-1 method and its mean AEP (MWh) over its feasible runs; n.s.: methods not significantly different from the best method (seed-paired Wilcoxon signed-rank, infeasible runs below every feasible run, Holm over its 12 comparisons, $\\alpha=0.05$). Scenarios: stored labels; $^a$in each scenario the open runs with the highest AEP of each exact-gradient method are taken as infeasible until only 15 of its 30 runs remain feasible (the lowest mean it can have while ranked by its mean); open exact infeas.: every open exact-gradient label taken as infeasible; + open MS-SLSQP: in addition every open label of MS-SLSQP with finite-difference gradients (fin.\\ diff.) taken as infeasible; ex.: exact gradient. Benchmark (68 cases, nine methods incl.\\ GA): with all 448 open MS-SLSQP labels infeasible (67 cases, at most 16 per case), MS-SLSQP has 78.0\\% feasible runs and fewer than 15 feasible runs in 1 case; average ranks PSO-VNS 2.18$\\to$2.18, PSO 2.40$\\to$2.40, GA 2.74$\\to$2.76, SSA-VNS 4.32$\\to$4.32, VNS 5.21$\\to$5.22, SSA 6.34$\\to$6.36, MS-SLSQP 6.85$\\to$6.76, LX-SSA 7.01$\\to$7.02, DE 7.96$\\to$7.96 (order unchanged); all-run outcome PSO-VNS vs.\\ MS-SLSQP 1649/218/173$\\to$1716/185/139 (wins/ties/losses). Horns Rev~1 pool (11 methods), open MS-SLSQP labels infeasible: 6{,}030 evaluations: 20 labels, MS-SLSQP 30$\\to$10 feasible runs, rank 8$\\to$10, best method PSO-VNS; 30{,}030 evaluations: 20 labels, MS-SLSQP 30$\\to$10 feasible runs, rank 8$\\to$10, best method GA. Budget and initialization studies: 22 case groups contain open MS-SLSQP labels; MS-SLSQP keeps at least half of its runs feasible in 18 of them and loses that qualification in 4 (Horns Rev~1).}"
  }
